From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 19:46:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP: Clear inherited driver context before adding a BSS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

setup_interface() preloads secondary BSSes with the primary BSS's
drv_priv and drv_owner_iface. If hostapd_if_add() fails before writing
its output pointer, the secondary BSS retains that borrowed context.

An observed failure during interface reuse reports:

  Could not set interface wlan0.2 flags (UP): No error information
  Failed to add BSS

For an MLD secondary BSS, the unwind can then remove the primary's
link through the inherited context and clear the primary's drv_priv.
Driver cleanup skips the primary, leaving nl80211 event callbacks
pointing at its freed hostapd_data.

Clear the secondary's inherited pointers immediately before if_add.
The primary remains the separate driver argument, and successful
creation supplies the secondary context and restores its owner. Keep
the existing-MLD borrowing branch ahead of this reset so that it still
reaches setup_mld with its borrowed context. Do not clear the output
after failure: the driver may already have published a new context.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ap/hostapd.c b/src/ap/hostapd.c
index 0ee85bc91d82..d4e66426e2f5 100644
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -1524,6 +1524,9 @@ static int hostapd_setup_bss(struct hostapd_data *hapd, int first,
 		}
 #endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 
+		/* if_add must supply this BSS's own driver context. */
+		hapd->drv_priv = NULL;
+		hapd->drv_owner_iface = NULL;
 		hapd->interface_added = 1;
 		if (hostapd_if_add(hapd->iface->bss[0], WPA_IF_AP_BSS,
 				   conf->iface, addr, hapd,
-- 
